      "writtenOn": "2022-06-28T03:16:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a particular advantage to using `MakeFromBackendRenderTarget` here instead of `MakeFromBackendTexture`? Since I structured this API to operate over any texture, perhaps the latter is more suitable but I don\u0027t know if there is a practical difference.\n\nbsalomon@: I experimented with `MakeFromBackendTexture` and `SkSurface::replaceBackendTexture` and the latter provides an approach to avoid creating a new Surface for every frame. I built a working prototype for `Surface.requestAnimationFrame` that is built around this and it can be a familiar alternative for `WebGPUCanvasContext.requestAnimationFrame` that I added.\n\nThis doesn\u0027t free the client from being careful about dealing with swapchain textures but it keeps the API for rendering multiple frames to one canvas similar to WebGL/SW versions.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 268,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 268,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "63ffbc6b79802ade50fbf11b5d66f34a7f78ae55",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "928eae57_3775824e",
        "filename": "modules/canvaskit/canvaskit_bindings.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 268,
      "author": {
        "id": 5085
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-06-28T14:40:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "MFBERT is mostly there to support GL FBOs, in particular FBO 0 which has no texture id. I think it\u0027s fine to use MFBET. The replaceBackendTexture idea is interesting. I could see how you could use that build an API that\u0027s more convenient to the client and more similar to WebGL/SW. I wouldn\u0027t directly expose replaceBackendTexture but maybe a higher level API that flushes, initiates the swap, and advances the surface to the next swap chain texture would make sense.",
      "parentUuid": "776d81bc_cbc4cdb5",
